Moving to Canada is a difficult thing to do when you are over 40, banking with RBC has been an absolutely NIGHTMARE but the biggest issue.......the Cream!

The UK and the rest of Europe has, unequivocally, the BEST dairy in the world. UK Double Cream is a dream, high fat, perfect consistency and very reasonably priced £0.38 per 100g ($0.65CAD).....yes you read that correctly. That's why I had a heart attack when the new machine arrived and put in a simple batch of ice cream using the highest fat standard cream here (33% whipping cream by Dairyland and $0.97 per 100g) and my heart sank as it is loaded with stabiliser and preservatives before you've even opened the carton. 
That's why I am going to find the best cream to make ice cream with here in Canada. 
Starting with today's pair of Dairyland Creams, the 33% Whipping Cream vs the 18% Coffee Cream. 
Next week is the turn of Lucerne brand, again I will use 33% whipping cream vs 18% coffee cream and finally, I will make the lxuxry cream versions using very expensive cream from Vital Green Farms vs Avalon 36% whipping cream (boucoup bucks btw). 

So lets see how much difference the cream actually makes to your ice cream as maybe you have many options in your country and want the best you can make. It might not be what you think!
